        "id": 1548775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T02:16:54Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "My understanding is that Zephyr should be working in the background to prevent shared interrupt lines from deasserting each other. But I\u0027ll admit I\u0027m not sure exactly how it works. I\u0027ve submitted a temporary patch to exclude yaviks from the tcpc driver until I can figure it out.",
      "parentUuid": "cbc5b41c_a7273afb",
      "revId": "5b5dee8e82c6c633d8efa92901d6100c0e4b846c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20159074_fbd05e18",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/nissa/xivu/src/usbc.c",
