        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T02:51:58Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "The issue is that these share a physical (open-drain) pin on the EC, so software has no control over it. A CPU interrupt will only occur the first time one of the devices asserts that signal, so one of them asserting it while the other is already holding it asserted isn\u0027t visible to the EC.\n\nI\u0027ve put up https://crrev.com/c/4252437 to disable the new shim handler for all nissa boards, because they\u0027re all subject to this problem.",
      "parentUuid": "7f4ee2cf_08d1027d",
      "revId": "5b5dee8e82c6c633d8efa92901d6100c0e4b846c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
